00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:18.780
<b>Warning Shots</b>

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:18.780
<b>Warning Shots</b>

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:34.120
Rey!

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.400
What are you doing?!

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.340
You're no better than a sitting duck flying like you are now!

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:40.660
This isn't your average engagement!

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:43.010
<i>What? What is this?</i>

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:52.640
{DO SOME THING}No air leaks. FCS contact.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:54.270
{DO SOMETHING}Minerva, all stations satisfactory.

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:56.380
{DO SOMETHING}Locate the enemy!

00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:58.400
Where are the Impulse and the Zaku?

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:01.990
One unidentified ship at Indigo 53, Mark 22, Bravo!

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:03.920
Distance 150!

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.040
That must be their mother ship.

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:08.680
Log the vessel into our database.

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:11.000
From now on, we'll refer to it as Bogey One.

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:15.170
Impulse and Zaku located at 157, Mark 80, Alpha.

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:17.230
They appear to be involved in a battle!

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:18.430
Can you call them?

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:21.340
No, ma'am. It's impossible with all the radio interference.

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:23.240
How many enemies?

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:24.230
One.

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:25.420
{split}However, it's...

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:26.970
...a mobile armor!

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:40.020
Rey!

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:50.710
We'll attack Bogey One! Lower the bridge!

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:53.170
Course, Indigo, Delta.

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:55.880
Accelerate twenty percent. {No don't move faster it hurts.}

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:59.380
Prepare to fire signal flares and anti-beam depth charges!

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:01.920
Arthur! What are you doing?!

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:03.380
Oh. I'm on it!

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:09.070
Load launcher eight, numbers one through four with Neidhardt!

00:04:09.070 --> 00:04:13.860
Activate Tristan one and two! Activate Isolde! Target: Bogey One!

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:19.310
Shouldn't our priority be to rescue them, Captain?

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:22.610
It is. That's why we're attacking their mother ship.

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:26.320
In this situation, the quickest way to save them is to push the enemy away.

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:32.710
Heat source approaching! Possible battleship!

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:36.130
Classification unknown! Red 53, Mark 80, Delta.

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:39.800
It's that new model of theirs.

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:43.030
Fifteen to starboard, accelerate thirty percent.

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:44.840
Activate Igelstellungs! Where's the Exus?

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:48.100
A ship?!

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:55.480
Those who try to take too much end up losing it all, I guess.

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:03.810
Minerva?

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:06.220
The retreat signal?! Why?!

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:07.320
It's an order.

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:09.280
Neidhardts, fire!

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:12.790
Evade!

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:33.220
Target their engines!

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:40.360
<i>The Exus has returned!</i>

00:05:41.050 --> 00:05:42.320
We're withdrawing, Lee!

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:48.150
Bogey One is retreating! Yellow 71 Alpha.

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:49.980
Where are the Impulse and the Zaku?

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:51.330
Returning. We're bringing them in now.

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:53.010
Make them hurry.

00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:55.710
{split}We'll pursue and eliminate Bogey One.

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:56.870
{split}Course heading Yellow Alpha.

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:09.550
Commander!

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:12.220
Sorry. Guess I got carried away.

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:14.010
Enemy ship still on our tail.

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:16.290
{split}Blue zero, distance 110.

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:18.020
It appears to be an awfully fast vessel.

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:19.690
{split}This could be trouble.

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:22.920
Missiles approaching!

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:24.110
Evade! Hard to port!

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:30.990
Detach extra propellant tanks from both sides, and detonate them!

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:33.910
No need to separate the arms! Let them have a taste of that!

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:38.330
Meanwhile, raise bow thirty-five, turn ten to port, maximum thrust!

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:47.890
Shinn!

00:06:47.890 --> 00:06:49.090
Hey. Is he all right?

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:00.900
Bogey One has detached a section of its hull!

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:05.050
Stop firing!

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:07.070
{split}Ten to starboard! Maximum thrust!

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:18.000
What is it?!

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:19.370
What now?

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:21.170
Bridge! What's going on?!

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:20.600
We're being bombed?

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:22.580
Damn it!

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:24.670
<i>All stations: Damage reports immediately!</i>

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:26.920
Bart. What's the enemy ship's position?

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:28.460
Wait one moment, I still haven't...

00:07:28.890 --> 00:07:32.000
Activate CIWS, fire anti-beam depth charges!

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:33.140
{split}They'll be firing at us next.

00:07:33.730 --> 00:07:37.340
Found it! Red 88, Mark 6, Charlie.

00:07:37.340 --> 00:07:38.980
Distance 500!

00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:40.430
Did they get away?!

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:43.840
Mr. Chairman?

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:44.770
Damn them!

00:07:45.350 --> 00:07:46.880
{split}Didn't think they'd use that to escape.

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.700
Seems to be one tough unit we're facing.

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:53.200
All the more reason why we mustn't let them get away.

00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:56.160
It'd be bad news if such a team got their hands on those machines.

00:07:56.850 --> 00:07:58.180
Right.

00:07:58.180 --> 00:08:00.620
At this point, it's too late to have you disembark

00:08:01.190 --> 00:08:04.740
and I believe it is best that we continue our pursuit of that ship.

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:06.540
What is your opinion on this, Mr. Chairman?

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:12.560
Don't worry about me, Captain.

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:14.390
Judging from that firepower,

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:19.930
it scares me to think of what might come later if we let them go now.

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:25.350
Right now, our top priority is to capture them, or to destroy them.

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:29.110
Thank you very much. Still have a trace on them?

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:30.300
We can still go after them.

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:35.830
Then this ship will resume its pursuit of Bogey One.

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:38.500
Course Yellow Alpha! Engines to maximum!

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:40.790
Course Yellow Alpha! Engines to maximum!

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.740
<i>Attention all hands.</i>

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:49.880
<i>This ship is commencing pursuit of Bogey One.</i>

00:08:50.870 --> 00:08:53.340
<i>Due to a sudden change in circumstances, this has become our maiden voyage</i>

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:56.100
<i>but the ship will be on a very important mission.</i>

00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:57.010
What?!

00:08:57.010 --> 00:09:01.390
<i>All hands, this is your opportunity to show what progress you've made during the daily training sessions.</i>

00:09:02.260 --> 00:09:04.020
Raise the bridge.

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:06.560
{split}Go to Condition Yellow until we enter a combat situation.

00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:08.320
Raising the bridge.

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:09.760
Going to Condition Yellow.

00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:12.190
Mr. Chairman. Please use the Captain's quarters to get some rest.

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:17.360
The Minerva prides itself on its speed, but the enemy vessel is also fast.

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:20.280
I don't imagine much will happen right away.

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:22.640
Rey. Please show him to his quarters.

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:22.950
Yes ma'am.

00:09:24.860 --> 00:09:25.950
<i>Captain!</i>

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:26.370
What is it?

00:09:26.890 --> 00:09:30.330
<i>Due to the battle, I was delayed in informing you about a situation.</i>

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:35.300
<i>During take off, we found two civilians aboard a Zaku in the hangar.</i>

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:35.590
What? {WHAT DO HERE}

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:39.050
<i>We detained the two, and found that one is</i>

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:42.500
<i>Representative Cagalli Yula Athha of the Orb Union,</i>

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:43.560
<i>and the other claims to be her attendant.</i>

00:09:44.360 --> 00:09:48.680
<i>They requested medical attention and a meeting with Chairman Durandal.</i>

00:09:48.680 --> 00:09:49.230
From Orb?

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:52.150
It's her. What's she doing on this ship?

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:55.760
<i>I acted on my own and arranged for the necessary medical care</i>

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:58.620
<i>and they are currently resting in the officers' quarters.</i>

00:10:35.720 --> 00:10:39.330
It looks like we've succeeded.

00:10:39.330 --> 00:10:41.050
How much longer till we reach point B?

00:10:41.050 --> 00:10:41.990
About two hours.

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:45.170
Do you think they will come after us?

00:10:45.170 --> 00:10:46.650
I don't know.

00:10:46.650 --> 00:10:50.370
I don't, so we should assume they will and continue along our planned route.

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:54.000
One should always assume the worst, right?

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:55.980
Especially on the battlefield.

00:10:58.000 --> 00:10:59.430
How about their recovery?

00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:04.260
They appear to be fine. They're sleeping like newborns.

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:09.800
However, I'm a little concerned that Auel used the block word on Stella.

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:12.900
I find that somewhat distressing.

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:17.980
Pilots that need to be returned to the cradle whenever something happens?

00:11:17.980 --> 00:11:20.570
Does the lab really believe they can be of use to us?

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:24.330
But they're a lot better than the previous group, don't you think?

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:27.840
They fully understand what we tell them and the work they're given.

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:35.790
It's a necessary evil. We're still in the trial stages in many regards.

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:38.740
This ship, the mobile suits, our pilots...

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:40.970
{split}and the world.

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:43.140
Yes, I understand.

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:47.470
The day will eventually come, when everything will begin in the true sense.

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:49.640
Under our name.

00:11:51.020 --> 00:11:56.400
What are you guys doing?! You've field stripped Zakus {merged}just fine during training!

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:58.360
It's exactly the same thing!

00:11:58.360 --> 00:11:59.320
Y-Yes, sir!

00:11:59.980 --> 00:12:02.200
But I still can't believe it.

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:05.060
Who would've expected we'd be in actual battle?

00:12:05.060 --> 00:12:06.110
Right.

00:12:06.110 --> 00:12:08.290
How did this happen so suddenly, anyway?

00:12:10.100 --> 00:12:15.760
This won't lead us straight into another war by any chance, will it?

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:16.880
I doubt it.

00:12:24.280 --> 00:12:26.010
I don't have the words to express my regret

00:12:27.020 --> 00:12:30.680
for involving you in this unfortunate situation.

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:33.140
However, Princess, please understand our position.

00:12:33.820 --> 00:12:37.270
Don't you know anything about that enemy unit yet?

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:40.630
Ah, well... I guess not.

00:12:40.630 --> 00:12:43.860
{split}We still have no information, not even on their carrier.

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:51.580
However, that's all the more reason why we must {merge}take control of the situation as soon as possible.

00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:54.460
Before it becomes too late.

00:12:55.180 --> 00:12:56.920
Yeah. I understand.

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:59.300
{split}Of course, Mr. Chairman.

00:12:59.860 --> 00:13:04.300
Right now, we must do everything we can to avoid upsetting the still fragile state of our world!

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:05.680
At any cost.

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:08.920
I knew you'd understand.

00:13:08.920 --> 00:13:12.600
I believed that you, Princess, would view the situation in that way.

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:19.940
If you'd like, I'd like to give you a tour of our ship while there's still time.

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:20.820
Mr. Chairman!

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:26.030
Although it's temporary, we are asking them to put their lives in our hands.

00:13:26.560 --> 00:13:30.450
This is the least that our nation can do for our allies, in good faith.

00:13:57.580 --> 00:13:58.730
Athha of Orb?!

00:13:59.120 --> 00:14:04.940
I was surprised too. What are the odds of meeting the hero of a major war here?

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:08.840
But why? Is there a problem with the Zaku?

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:09.700
Ah, no.

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:12.820
The machine hadn't been assigned to the Minerva.

00:14:12.820 --> 00:14:14.700
So I was curious who was piloting it.

00:14:15.440 --> 00:14:18.770
Actually, it seems that it was her escort piloting it.

00:14:18.770 --> 00:14:20.580
He said his name's Alex.

00:14:21.580 --> 00:14:23.500
But... he could be Athrun.

00:14:25.280 --> 00:14:28.430
That's what the Representative called him. In the heat of the moment.

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:30.550
She called him Athrun.

00:14:33.380 --> 00:14:36.890
Athrun Zala. It's rumored that he lives in Orb now, right?

00:14:37.820 --> 00:14:39.760
Athrun... Zala.

00:14:40.960 --> 00:14:44.610
But this ship has certainly gotten itself involved in something incredible!

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:50.450
To have to fight in an actual battle the day before its own launch ceremony?

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:54.870
We'll take this lift up to the mobile suit deck.

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:05.130
Think of this section as being the core of the ship.

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:09.630
I am not at liberty to tell you how many the ship can hold,

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:12.470
but I can tell you we aren't at full capacity.

00:15:18.060 --> 00:15:23.010
I've taken you've already me the Z GMF-1000, the Zaku.

00:15:23.010 --> 00:15:25.320
It's currently the main machine of ZAFT.

00:15:27.080 --> 00:15:32.410
And then there's the Impulse that utilizes the launch system, arguably the main feature of the Minerva.

00:15:33.300 --> 00:15:35.610
I understand you had a chance to see it at the factory.

00:15:35.610 --> 00:15:36.580
Ah, yes.

00:15:37.230 --> 00:15:43.710
Apparently, according to the scientists, this is an brand new, highly efficient mobile suit system.

00:15:44.680 --> 00:15:47.920
I don't claim to be an expert on the technical aspects however.

00:15:50.100 --> 00:15:53.590
But I take it that the Princess does not much care for this.

00:15:54.140 --> 00:15:56.000
You seem awfully happy about it, Mr. Chairman.

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:58.600
I wouldn't call this glee.

00:15:59.840 --> 00:16:03.110
I am simply proud of everyone's earnest work,

00:16:03.110 --> 00:16:07.490
and to have come this far and gain this much power...

00:16:07.490 --> 00:16:08.780
Power...

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:13.940
You said that power is necessary because there will always be conflict, Mr. Chairman.

00:16:14.560 --> 00:16:14.950
Yes.

00:16:15.550 --> 00:16:18.950
Then, how do you explain what happened here?!

00:16:19.550 --> 00:16:21.910
The damage suffered by your nation

00:16:22.400 --> 00:16:24.370
as a result of just those three new model mobile suits!

00:16:25.020 --> 00:16:25.790
Representative!

00:16:26.180 --> 00:16:29.670
So you're saying that's reason enough to remain powerless?

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:34.120
Why are such things necessary in the first place?! Why now?!

00:16:34.900 --> 00:16:38.780
We made a pledge not to repeat the tragedies of the past!

00:16:38.780 --> 00:16:40.970
We were committed to following a path that we could proceed along hand in hand!

00:16:41.360 --> 00:16:43.900
Well... Consider this, Princess...

00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:46.650
More of that idealistic crap the Athhas are so famous for!

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:49.230
Shinn!

00:16:49.630 --> 00:16:50.860
Shinn!

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:02.370
We've caught up with Bogey One.

00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:05.290
Orange 55, Mark 90, Alpha.

00:17:05.890 --> 00:17:09.250
Large heat source located at Yellow 50, Mark 82, Charlie!

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:10.920
Distance 8000.

00:17:11.540 --> 00:17:13.340
<i>Located enemy vessel. Distance 8000.</i>

00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:18.040
<i>Condition Red announced! Pilots, standby in your machines!</i>

00:17:18.040 --> 00:17:20.600
Hurry with the final checks! It's starting!

00:17:20.960 --> 00:17:22.100
Oh, no.

00:17:24.360 --> 00:17:25.160
Shinn!

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:31.200
I'm very sorry, Mr. Chairman. He will be punished for his actions later!

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:35.570
I'm terribly sorry, Princess.

00:17:36.140 --> 00:17:38.030
He's an immigrant from Orb,

00:17:39.160 --> 00:17:42.280
so that was the last thing I expected to come out of him.

00:17:47.660 --> 00:17:48.750
They came after all.

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:53.420
Yeah. Well, it goes to show that ZAFT aren't twiddling their thumbs.

00:17:54.240 --> 00:17:55.340
We're going to crush them!

00:17:55.890 --> 00:17:59.300
All hands to battle stations! Pilots are to proceed to the briefing room!

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:03.220
I don't expect the enemy to deliberately proceed into the debris,

00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:06.140
but this is nevertheless a dangerous battleground.

00:18:06.590 --> 00:18:08.230
Helm. We're counting on you.

00:18:08.230 --> 00:18:08.810
Yes, ma'am!

00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:11.870
We'll send out Shinn and Lunamaria first.

00:18:11.870 --> 00:18:13.280
{split}Is the crew ready?

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:13.960
Yes, ma'am!

00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:15.900
6500 to target!

00:18:17.880 --> 00:18:18.800
Mr. Chairman!

00:18:19.340 --> 00:18:20.490
May I have a word, Captain?

00:18:21.440 --> 00:18:25.870
I'd like to invite our guests from Orb to join us on the bridge.

00:18:26.180 --> 00:18:29.560
Huh? Ah, but, that's...

00:18:29.560 --> 00:18:33.500
As you're well aware, the Representative took command of a battleship during the previous war

00:18:34.350 --> 00:18:37.470
and has a long experience in warfare.

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:42.890
I'd like to have her perspective as she observes our combat methods.

00:18:44.120 --> 00:18:45.340
Very well.

00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:48.360
{split}If that's how you feel, Mr. Chairman.

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:50.560
Thank you, Talia.

00:18:53.860 --> 00:18:55.030
6000 to target!

00:18:55.400 --> 00:18:59.150
Lower the bridge! Prepare for battle against a battleship and mobile suits.

00:19:02.140 --> 00:19:04.200
That new model vessel?

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:07.380
Yeah. I wonder if we'll see that combining fellow again.

00:19:07.380 --> 00:19:10.530
Then this time we'll be sure to either break him apart or capture him.

00:19:10.530 --> 00:19:13.340
In either case, we're gonna have some fun again.

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:14.820
Stella?

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:29.020
Cast anchor! Cut engines after firing! Launch decoy!

00:19:30.300 --> 00:19:31.650
Don't mess up the timing.

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:51.470
<i>Lunamaria Hawke, Zaku Warrior, standby for launch.</i>

00:19:51.470 --> 00:19:55.180
<i>All systems online. Commencing launch sequence.</i>

00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:08.200
<i>Standby to launch Impulse. Blast module selected.</i>

00:20:08.200 --> 00:20:10.660
<i>Silhouette Hangar number three to be released.</i>

00:20:11.380 --> 00:20:15.810
<i>Platform setup is complete. Central catapult online.</i>

00:20:15.810 --> 00:20:20.890
<i>Opening airtight shutters. Core Splendor, all systems online.</i>

00:20:20.890 --> 00:20:22.950
<i>Commencing takeoff sequence.</i>

00:20:23.620 --> 00:20:26.780
<i>Hatch opened. Linear launch system engaged.</i>

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:33.420
Target, on our present course. Distance 4700.

00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:36.080
Zaku, Impulse! Launch!

00:20:37.180 --> 00:20:40.460
<i>More of that idealistic crap the Athhas are so famous for!</i>

00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:42.840
<i>He's an immigrant from Orb...</i>

00:20:47.620 --> 00:20:50.680
<i>Gunner Zaku Warrior, catapult engaged.</i>

00:20:55.220 --> 00:20:58.650
Lunamaria Hawke, Zaku! I'm taking off!

00:21:04.620 --> 00:21:06.320
Bogey One...

00:21:06.920 --> 00:21:11.240
I wonder what that ship's real name is.

00:21:12.720 --> 00:21:14.660
<i>You're next, Impulse. Go ahead!</i>

00:21:16.140 --> 00:21:19.040
Shinn Asuka, Core Splendor! Taking off!

00:21:52.780 --> 00:21:54.750
The name of a thing is an indicator of its existence.

00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:59.440
Then what if that name is not real?

00:22:03.900 --> 00:22:09.930
If it's not real,  would that mean its existence is not real either?

00:22:10.610 --> 00:22:12.390
Is that what it would mean?

00:22:13.760 --> 00:22:15.430
Alex... Or rather...

00:22:16.280 --> 00:22:17.820
Athrun Zala.

00:22:18.400 --> 00:22:25.820
<b>kotoba wo kasanete mo wakari aenai koto</b>

00:22:18.400 --> 00:22:25.820
I still did not realize

00:22:25.110 --> 00:22:32.620
<b>
mada shiranakatta ne</b>

00:22:25.110 --> 00:22:32.620
That there are things that can't be conveyed even with words

00:22:31.910 --> 00:22:40.250
<b>kimi dake wo dakishimetakute nakushita yume kimi wa</b>

00:22:31.910 --> 00:22:40.250
My lost dreams of wanting to hold you by my side,

00:22:39.580 --> 00:22:47.220
<b>
"akiramenaide" to itta</b>

00:22:39.580 --> 00:22:47.220
For them, you said, "Don't give up!"

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:54.060
<b>tooku hanareteru hodo ni chikaku ni kanjiteru</b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:54.060
The further we are apart, the nearer I feel you are

00:22:53.350 --> 00:23:02.190
<b>
samishisa mo tsuyosa eto kawatteku... kimi wo omottanara</b>

00:22:53.350 --> 00:23:02.190
Even my loneliness turns into strength... when I think of you

00:23:01.520 --> 00:23:08.900
<b>setsunaku mune wo sasu sore wa yume no kakera</b>

00:23:01.520 --> 00:23:08.900
The thing that pierces the gentle chest, that's a fragment of my dream

00:23:08.190 --> 00:23:21.880
<b>
arinomama deaeteta sono kiseki mou ichido shinjite</b>

00:23:08.190 --> 00:23:21.880
Believe once more in the the miracle that is our chanced meeting

00:23:22.000 --> 00:23:23.920
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:22.000 --> 00:23:23.920
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:25.520 --> 00:23:27.090
Is it because there is power?

00:23:28.090 --> 00:23:29.300
Is it because there is conflict?

00:23:30.680 --> 00:23:35.140
Through endless time, the answer has yet to be found,

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:39.430
however desired it is in the situation encountered...

00:23:41.440 --> 00:23:45.070
Next, on Mobile Suit Gundam Seed Destiny,

00:23:45.070 --> 00:23:46.500
"Stardust Battlefield."

00:23:45.980 --> 00:23:51.950
<b>Next time</b>

00:23:45.980 --> 00:23:51.950
<b>Next time</b>

00:23:45.980 --> 00:23:51.950
<b>Stardust Battlefield</b>

00:23:45.980 --> 00:23:51.950
<b>Stardust Battlefield</b>

00:23:47.560 --> 00:23:50.040
Show off that strength of yours, Zaku!
